--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The numbers inside `data/published/` are not ours, and we cannot license
them to you. They are statistics and published prices produced by Eurostat,
the European Central Bank, the Bulgarian National Bank (БНБ), the Bulgarian
National Statistical Institute (НСИ) and имот.bg, which this project
retrieves and republishes with attribution.

We never held the right to license those figures out, and the Apache
Licence in `LICENSE` does not purport to grant you any right in them. They
remain subject to each publisher's own terms, and each publisher's terms —
not ours — govern what you may do with them.

**Every published payload carries a `source_url` naming its origin.** That
field exists for exactly this reason: to identify who a figure belongs to,
and whom to ask.

Our own contribution to those files — the schema, the field names, the
envelope, the provenance blocks, the chosen aggregations and the labelling
— is covered by the Apache Licence like the rest of the code.

The publishers' terms differ from one another, and at least one of them
restricts the redistribution of derived and composite works. Before you
reuse a figure, identify its publisher from the `source_url` it carries and
read that publisher's own terms. What each publisher permits — quoted
verbatim, in the original language, and dated — is recorded in
`docs/data-sources.md` and `docs/legal.md`.

This is not a formality. If you fork this repository and redistribute
`data/published/`, the upstream terms travel with the figures and become
your responsibility, not ours.


